A **relic** is a new kind of record in Workbook, separate from tasks. It holds a title, a type, an author, links, and content made of named **parts**.

- Workbook stores relics in Git, shares them through `origin`, and keeps every change, as it does for tasks.
- Workbook enforces a small set of fields. Each project defines everything else with a schema kept in the shared project settings.
- Workbook ships default schemas for specs and plans, so a new or upgraded project has a working shape from the first day.
- A relic or one of its parts can link to tasks and to other relics or their parts.
- Two people editing the same text are merged automatically where possible. A real conflict goes to the acting agent.
- Workbook is the place the data lives. Skills and viewers built on top decide what a relic looks like.
